msgid "Analyse frequencies"
msgstr "▁Fréquences d'analyse"

msgid "As a fraction of the signal's full range. 0.1 keeps peaks standing at least a tenth of the range above their surroundings."
msgstr "▁Comme une fraction de la▁gamme▁complète du signal. 0.1▁maintient les▁pics▁debout au▁moins un▁dixième de la▁gamme au-dessus de▁leur▁environnement."

msgid "Asymmetry. Smaller pushes the baseline further below the peaks; it should stay well under 0.5."
msgstr "Asymétrie. Plus▁petite▁pousse le▁niveau de base plus▁loin▁sous les▁pics; il▁devrait▁rester bien en▁dessous de 0,5."

msgid "Baseline"
msgstr "▁Données de▁référence"

msgid "Between samples"
msgstr "▁Entre les▁échantillons"

msgid "Choose a decomposition (a curve per component) or a manifold embedding (a 2D scatter)."
msgstr "▁Choisissez une▁décomposition (une▁courbe par▁composant) ou un▁incrustation multiple (une dispersion 2D)."

msgid "Choose the baseline estimator."
msgstr "▁Choisissez l'estimateur de base."

msgid "Choose the spectral or correlation estimator."
msgstr "▁Choisissez l'estimateur spectral ou de▁corrélation."

msgid "Component"
msgstr "▁Composante"

msgid "Component 1"
msgstr "▁Composante 1"

msgid "Component 2"
msgstr "▁Composante 2"

msgid "Components"
msgstr "▁Composantes"

msgid "Convert to decibels"
msgstr "▁Convertir en▁décibels"

msgid "Cubic spline"
msgstr "▁Épingle cubique"

msgid "Curve"
msgstr "Courbe"

msgid "Damping (sigma)"
msgstr "Abattage (sigma)"

msgid "Damping sigma of the Laplace variable s = sigma + i*omega. Zero reduces the transform to the Fourier transform; increasing it weights early samples more and suppresses late ones, which is what makes a decaying or unstable signal integrable."
msgstr "Amortir la sigma de la variable Laplace s = sigma + i*omega. Zéro▁réduit la transformation à la transformation de Fourier; l'augmenter▁pèse plus▁tôt les▁échantillons et▁supprime les▁derniers, ce qui▁rend un signal en▁décomposition ou▁instable▁intégrable."

msgid "Decompose or embed several series together (PCA, ICA, NMF, t-SNE, ...)"
msgstr "Décomposer ou▁intégrer▁plusieurs▁séries ensemble (PCA, ICA, NMF, t-SNE, ...)"

msgid "Detrend"
msgstr "Dépendance"

msgid "Direction"
msgstr "Direction"

msgid "Draw the estimated baseline itself."
msgstr "▁Dessinez la base de▁référence▁estimée▁elle-même."

msgid "Estimates"
msgstr "▁Prévisions"

msgid "Every selected series is linearly resampled onto this many evenly spaced points across their shared x range, before decomposing or embedding them together."
msgstr "▁Chaque▁série▁sélectionnée est rééchantillonnée▁linéairement sur▁ces▁nombreux points▁uniformément espacés sur▁leur▁plage de x▁partagée,▁avant de les▁décomposer ou de les▁intégrer ensemble."

msgid "Explained variance"
msgstr "variance▁expliquée"

msgid "Express the result as 10*log10 of the value."
msgstr "▁Exprimez le▁résultat en 10*log10 de la▁valeur."

msgid "Filter by"
msgstr "▁Filtrer par"

msgid "Find"
msgstr "▁Rechercher"

msgid "Find and measure peaks"
msgstr "▁Trouver et▁mesurer les▁pics"

msgid "Find where a series crosses a level"
msgstr "▁Trouver▁où une▁série▁traverse un▁niveau"

msgid "Fold the negative frequencies onto the positive ones. Correct for real-valued signals."
msgstr "Pliez les▁fréquences▁négatives sur les▁fréquences▁positives. Correct pour les▁signaux▁réels."

msgid "Found on the surface's own exact x/y grid."
msgstr "Trouvé sur la▁propre▁grille x/y▁exacte de la surface."

msgid "Fraction of each segment shared with the next."
msgstr "Fraction de▁chaque segment▁partagée avec le▁prochain."

msgid "Grid points"
msgstr "Points de▁grille"

msgid "Half-prominence bounds"
msgstr "▁Limites de la▁demi-prominence"

msgid "Height (absolute)"
msgstr "▁Hauteur (absolue)"

msgid "How each bracketed crossing is refined. The three bracketing solvers cannot leave the interval they were given; Newton can, and is checked afterwards."
msgstr "Comment▁chaque▁croisement entre▁crochets est▁affiné. Les▁trois résolveurs ne▁peuvent▁pas▁laisser l'intervalle▁qu'ils▁ont▁été▁donnés; Newton▁peut, et est▁vérifié par la suite."

msgid "How many components to extract. Clamped to the number of selected series."
msgstr "▁Combien de▁composants à▁extraire. Clampé au nombre de▁séries▁sélectionnées."

msgid "How many decimal places of x the solver has to settle before it stops. Nine is far below the precision of any measured x; the cost of raising it is a few iterations."
msgstr "▁Combien de▁décimales de x le▁solveur▁doit se▁régler▁avant▁qu'il ne s'arrête.▁Neuf est bien en▁dessous de la▁précision de n'importe▁quel x▁mesuré; le▁coût de l'élévation est▁quelques itérations."

msgid "How many nearby points each one is connected to. Lowered automatically if it does not fit the sample count."
msgstr "▁Combien de points à▁proximité▁chacun est▁connecté. Abaissé▁automatiquement s'il ne correspond▁pas au nombre d'échantillons."

msgid "How many scales to evaluate between the longest period the record supports and the Nyquist frequency, spaced logarithmically."
msgstr "▁Combien d'échelles à▁évaluer entre la plus▁longue▁période▁prise en charge par l'enregistrement et la▁fréquence Nyquist, espacée logarithmiquement."

msgid "Input"
msgstr "▁Entrée"

msgid "Iterations"
msgstr "Itérations"

msgid "Keeps the first crossings in x order when a noisy series crosses the level hundreds of times."
msgstr "Conserve les▁premiers▁passages dans l'ordre x▁quand une▁série▁bruyante▁traverse le▁niveau des▁centaines de▁fois."

msgid "Keeps the most prominent peaks when many are found."
msgstr "Conserve les▁pics les plus proéminents▁quand▁beaucoup▁sont▁trouvés."

msgid "Kind"
msgstr "▁Genre"

msgid "Lambda"
msgstr "Lambda"

msgid "Largest lag to keep. 0 keeps every lag."
msgstr "Le plus grand▁décalage à▁garder. 0▁garde▁tous les▁décalages."

msgid "Level"
msgstr "▁Niveau"

msgid "Max lags"
msgstr "Laps de▁temps maximum"

msgid "Maximum iterations"
msgstr "Échéance▁maximale"

msgid "Method"
msgstr "▁Méthode"

msgid "Minimum"
msgstr "▁Durée▁minimale"

msgid "Minimum separation"
msgstr "Séparation▁minimale"

msgid "Minimum width"
msgstr "▁Largeur▁minimale"

msgid "Model"
msgstr "▁Modèle"

msgid "Monotone cubic (PCHIP)"
msgstr "Monotone cubique (PCHIP)"

msgid "Morlet central frequency w0. Higher values resolve frequency more finely at the cost of time resolution; 6 is the usual compromise and the value at which the wavelet is near-admissible."
msgstr "Morlet▁fréquence▁centrale w0. Des▁valeurs plus▁élevées résolvent la▁fréquence plus finement au▁prix de la▁résolution du▁temps; 6 est le▁compromis▁habituel et la▁valeur à▁laquelle l'ondelette est▁presque admissible."

msgid "Morlet w0"
msgstr "Morlet w0"

msgid "Neighbors"
msgstr "▁Voisins"

msgid "No peaks passed the filter. Lower the minimum, or switch from height to prominence if the baseline is not at zero."
msgstr "▁Aucun▁pic n'a▁franchi le▁filtre. Abaissez le minimum, ou▁passez de la▁hauteur à la proéminence si la▁ligne de base n'est▁pas à▁zéro."

msgid "No results."
msgstr "▁Aucun▁résultat."

msgid "Normalisation"
msgstr "Normalisation"

msgid "One-sided spectrum"
msgstr "▁spectre unidirectionnel"

msgid "Peak ({x} &rarr; {y})"
msgstr "Cap ({x} &rarr; {y})"

msgid "Peaks, baseline correction, spectral analysis, decomposition and roots, with the spectrogram chart."
msgstr "Les▁pics, la correction de base, l'analyse spectrale, la▁décomposition et les▁racines, avec le▁graphique spectrogramme."

msgid "Per crossing. Brent and TOMS 748 rarely need ten; the limit is what stops a pathological bracket from hanging the dialog."
msgstr "Par▁croisement. Brent et TOMS 748▁ont▁rarement▁besoin de▁dix; la▁limite est ce qui▁empêche un support pathologique de▁suspendre le dialogue."

msgid "Perplexity"
msgstr "Perplexité"

msgid "Points"
msgstr "▁Remarques"

msgid "Points at half prominence. Raise it to reject single-sample spikes, which are usually instrument artefacts rather than features."
msgstr "Points à▁moitié en▁évidence. Levez-le pour▁rejeter les▁pics à un▁seul▁échantillon, qui▁sont▁généralement des artefacts d'instrument▁plutôt que des▁caractéristiques."

msgid "Points. Of any two peaks closer than this, the more prominent is kept - which is how a single noisy peak stops being reported as several."
msgstr "Points.▁Parmi les▁deux▁pics plus▁proches, les plus proéminents▁sont▁maintenus - c'est▁ainsi▁qu'un▁seul▁pic▁bruyant▁cesse d'être▁signalé▁comme▁plusieurs."

msgid "Prominence"
msgstr "Prominence"

msgid "Prominence (relative)"
msgstr "Prominence (relative)"

msgid "Prominence measures a peak against its own surroundings and survives a sloping baseline. Height compares it to zero, which only means something when the baseline is at zero."
msgstr "La prominence▁mesure un▁pic par▁rapport à son▁propre▁environnement et survit à une base en▁pente. La▁hauteur la compare à▁zéro, ce qui▁signifie▁seulement▁quelque chose▁lorsque la base est à▁zéro."

msgid "Re-weighting passes."
msgstr "Les▁passes de repondération."

msgid "Remove a constant or linear trend from each segment first. A trend leaks into the lowest frequency bins and hides everything near it."
msgstr "Enlevez d'abord une▁tendance▁constante ou▁linéaire de▁chaque segment.▁Une▁tendance s'écoule dans les▁bacs de▁fréquence les plus bas et cache▁tout à▁proximité."

msgid "Report at most"
msgstr "Signaler au maximum"

msgid "Residual"
msgstr "Résidus"

msgid "Roughly, how many neighbours each point is assumed to have. Lowered automatically if it does not fit the sample count."
msgstr "En▁gros,▁combien de▁voisins▁chaque point est▁supposé▁avoir. Abaissé▁automatiquement s'il ne correspond▁pas au nombre d'échantillons."

msgid "Samples per Welch segment. Longer segments resolve finer frequency detail; shorter ones average away more noise."
msgstr "Des▁échantillons par segment▁Welch. Des segments plus▁longs résolvent des▁détails de▁fréquence plus▁fins; les plus courts font plus de▁bruit en▁moyenne."

msgid "Scales"
msgstr "Échelles"

msgid "Scaling"
msgstr "▁Étalonnage"

msgid "Segment length"
msgstr "▁Longueur du segment"

msgid "Segment overlap"
msgstr "Recoupement des segments"

msgid "Select one or more source series."
msgstr "▁Sélectionnez une ou▁plusieurs▁séries sources."

msgid "Series"
msgstr "▁Série"

msgid "Signal analysis"
msgstr "Analyse des▁signaux"

msgid "Smoothness. Larger makes the baseline stiffer, so it bends less to follow narrow peaks."
msgstr "La▁douceur. Plus▁grande▁rend la▁ligne de base plus▁rigide, de▁sorte▁qu'il▁penche▁moins pour▁suivre des▁pics▁étroits."

msgid "Solver"
msgstr "Solveur"

msgid "Source"
msgstr "Source"

msgid "Straight line"
msgstr "▁Ligne▁droite"

msgid "Subtract a spectrum's background (AsLS or rubber band)"
msgstr "▁Soustraire le fond d'un▁spectre (ASLS ou▁bande de▁caoutchouc)"

msgid "Taper applied to each segment before the FFT."
msgstr "Taper▁appliqué à▁chaque segment▁avant le FFT."

msgid "The series never crosses this level. Check the level against the data's range - a crossing no two samples straddle cannot be found from these samples."
msgstr "La▁série ne▁traverse▁jamais ce▁niveau.▁Vérifiez le▁niveau par▁rapport à la▁plage de▁données - un▁croisement▁aucun▁deux▁échantillons▁chevauchent ne▁peut▁être▁trouvé à▁partir de▁ces▁échantillons."

msgid "The surface never reaches this level - z stays on one side of it everywhere on the grid."
msgstr "La surface n'atteint▁jamais ce▁niveau - z▁reste d'un▁côté de▁celui-ci▁partout sur la▁grille."

msgid "The y value to solve for. 0 finds the zeros; any other value finds where the series crosses that level, which is the same problem shifted."
msgstr "La▁valeur y à▁résoudre pour. 0▁trouve les▁zéros;▁toute▁autre▁valeur▁trouve▁où la▁série▁croise ce▁niveau, qui est le▁même▁problème▁déplacé."

msgid "This surface's points were not a complete x/y grid, so the peaks below were found on a linearly interpolated one - treat them as approximate."
msgstr "Les points de▁cette surface n'étaient▁pas une▁grille▁complète x/y, de▁sorte que les▁pics ci-dessous▁ont▁été▁trouvés sur un interpolé▁linéairement - les▁traiter▁comme▁approximatives."

msgid "This surface's points were not a complete x/y grid, so this level curve was traced on a linearly interpolated one - treat it as approximate."
msgstr "Les points de▁cette surface n'étaient▁pas une▁grille▁complète x/y,▁donc▁cette▁courbe de▁niveau a▁été▁tracée sur une▁courbe interpolée▁linéairement - la▁traiter▁comme▁approximative."

msgid "Tolerance (digits)"
msgstr "Tolérance (chiffres)"

msgid "Traced on the surface's own exact x/y grid."
msgstr "Tracé sur la▁propre▁grille x/y▁exacte de la surface."

msgid "Variance share"
msgstr "Part des▁écarts"

msgid "What the series is assumed to do between two points. Linear claims nothing the samples do not; the two curved options fit a smooth signal better and can overshoot a noisy one into crossings that are not there."
msgstr "Ce que la▁série est▁supposé▁faire entre▁deux points. Linear ne▁prétend▁rien que les▁échantillons ne font▁pas; les▁deux options▁courbes s'adaptent▁mieux à un signal▁lisse et▁peuvent▁dépasser un▁bruyant dans des▁passages qui ne▁sont▁pas▁là."

msgid "Which turning points to look for."
msgstr "▁Quels▁tournants à▁rechercher."

msgid "Width"
msgstr "▁Largeur"

msgid "Window"
msgstr "Fenêtre"

msgid "density: power per unit frequency. spectrum: power per segment."
msgstr "▁densité:▁puissance par▁unité de▁fréquence.▁spectre:▁puissance par segment."

msgid "falling"
msgstr "▁chute"

msgid "level {level}"
msgstr "▁niveau {level}"

msgid "maximum"
msgstr "maximum"

msgid "minimum"
msgstr "minimum"

msgid "p"
msgstr "p"

msgid "rising"
msgstr "la▁hausse"

